Each assertion has exactly one producing work unit and one guarding evidence obligation.
No assertion is satisfied incidentally.

**Carried defect in the gate (DESIGN §5.5, surfaced not worked around).** The regex
`^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$` admits `[0.00, 0.99]` and **cannot express `1.00`** — total
extraction failure, the strongest possible falsification of A8, is unrepresentable by the
gate that commissioned the probe. Handling, in priority order: (1) `1.00` is unreachable
whenever G5 holds and PAEOS emits anything at all, and if `N = 0` then G5 fails first and
the verdict is already NO-GO; (2) if the computed value lands ≥ 0.995, clamp per WU-5 with
`loss_ratio_note` and the exact value in the body; (3) report the defect to the gate author
in report §4. Fabricating a representable number without saying so is the one failure mode
that would make the whole probe untrustworthy, and it is forbidden.

